From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolò Veronese <nicveronese@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: Create device link to external PHY referenced by
 phy-handle

When a DSA switch port references an external PHY (e.g. the Airoha
EN8811H 2.5G PHY) via phy-handle, and that PHY's driver defers its
probe (firmware not yet available), the -EPROBE_DEFER propagation in
dsa_tree_setup_ports() alone causes a self-reinforcing deferred-probe
feedback loop: every switch re-probe re-registers the internal MDIO
bus and PHYs, each internal PHY binding fires
driver_deferred_probe_trigger(), and the switch is re-probed
immediately (~520ms per cycle, flooding the log and stalling boot).

Create a managed device link from the switch to the external PHY
during port DT parsing. The link carries DL_FLAG_AUTOPROBE_CONSUMER
(NOT DL_FLAG_SYNC_STATE_ONLY, which fw_devlink uses in permissive
mode and which device_links_check_suppliers ignores), so after the
first failed probe the driver core defers subsequent switch probes in
really_probe() -> device_links_check_suppliers() WITHOUT calling the
switch driver's ->probe(). The internal MDIO bus is therefore never
re-registered and the loop cannot sustain itself.

When the PHY finally binds (firmware loaded), the device link
triggers an automatic switch re-probe via device_links_driver_bound()
and the tree comes up normally.

Complements pending-6.18/704 ("net: dsa: support EPROBE_DEFER when
reading the port MAC address"), which propagates -EPROBE_DEFER from
dsa_port_setup() through dsa_tree_setup_ports().

--- a/net/dsa/dsa.c
+++ b/net/dsa/dsa.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <linux/rtnetlink.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_net.h>
+#include <linux/of_mdio.h>
 #include <net/dsa_stubs.h>
 #include <net/sch_generic.h>
 
@@ -1243,11 +1244,24 @@ static int dsa_port_parse_cpu(struct dsa
 static int dsa_port_parse_of(struct dsa_port *dp, struct device_node *dn)
 {
 	struct device_node *ethernet = of_parse_phandle(dn, "ethernet", 0);
+	struct device_node *phy_np;
 	const char *name = of_get_property(dn, "label", NULL);
 	bool link = of_property_read_bool(dn, "link");
 
 	dp->dn = dn;
 
+	phy_np = of_parse_phandle(dn, "phy-handle", 0);
+	if (phy_np) {
+		struct phy_device *phydev = of_phy_find_device(phy_np);
+
+		if (phydev) {
+			device_link_add(dp->ds->dev, &phydev->mdio.dev,
+					DL_FLAG_AUTOPROBE_CONSUMER);
+			put_device(&phydev->mdio.dev);
+		}
+		of_node_put(phy_np);
+	}
+
 	if (ethernet) {
 		struct net_device *conduit;
 		const char *user_protocol;
